Output is `{"name":"Jane","age":30}` ✅

Here's the complete `Program.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase };
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Jane", 30), options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

The key piece is `JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` — pass it via `JsonSerializerOptions` to convert PascalCase properties (`Name`, `Age`) to camelCase (`name`, `age`). The record type must appear **after** the top-level statements in C#.
